  "sourceNotes": "The watch cap (or stocking cap) is a military knitting staple. Weldon's Practical Knitter Series 1 (1886) describes close-fitting rib caps for sailors. Mary Thomas's Knitting Book (1938) p. 82 discusses short watchcap construction.",
